# App shell (src-tauri)

## Composition (lib.rs)

`compose()` builds every adapter, `WarRoomService::new(Ports{…})`, `restore()` (events), then spawns:
transcript first read (thread), socket ingress (tokio), the 5 s `tick` (liveness, transcripts of
working sessions, stall detection) and the notification-actions loop. Closing the window hides it.

## Contract with the front

Commands in `commands.rs` (blocking work through `blocking()` = `spawn_blocking`); events in
`adapters.rs` / `lib.rs`: `warroom://view`, `warroom://open-detail` (`{id, reply}`), `pty://output`,
`pty://exit`. **Names and argument names are mirrored in `src/infrastructure/tauriGateway.ts`**: change
both or neither.

## Tray, notifications, instance

- Tray: lamp colored by aggregate attention (generated RGBA, no assets), tooltip with counters, menu
  "next / open / quit".
- Notifications (`adapters.rs::DesktopNotifier`, `notify-rust`): one per session (stable id replaces
  the previous), NeedsYou = critical + no timeout. Buttons: View, Go to, Approve (if approvable),
  Reply. Freedesktop has **no inline reply** (notify-rust says so): "Reply" opens the preview
  with the message box focused.
- Single instance: a second launch forwards argv; `--next` jumps to what has waited longest
  (`go_next`), used from a KDE global shortcut. `--hidden` comes from autostart.

